      "side": 1,
      "message": "This bug seems to be yet another proof that we\u0027d better properly track _devices_ in some data structure on pKVM side (possibly just reusing `struct device_domain_info`), like we already properly track domains. I.e. build our context/PASID hypercalls API around such a _device_ abstraction, instead of expecting the host to pass all these isolated values of `bus`, `devfn`, `iommu`, `ats_qdep` etc every time and manually coupling them together and validating them for consistency in every place in error-prone ways, or manually parsing `pasid_table` or `ats_supported` from context tables every time, and so on and so forth.",
      "revId": "159ee8f797fc3e16406f9e38905439d59c45ec62",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
