      "writtenOn": "2026-07-23T20:51:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ack.\nWe did have one data structure for tracking devices in pkvm in the earliest shadow table implementation, but it came up with a lot of un-needed code like tracking device life times and all (get/put/alloc/free etc.) which made the code unnecessarily complicated and hard to understand, so we got rid of it but will have to bring it for the device passthrough.",
      "parentUuid": "77b20e59_5f360c47",
      "revId": "159ee8f797fc3e16406f9e38905439d59c45ec62",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bfd20dc2_a359e669",
